\section{Semi-Analytic Yukawa Overlaps}

The overlap between modes on bridges separated by distance \(d_{ij}\) admits the expansion
\[
Y_{ij}\approx C\exp\left(-\frac{d_{ij}}{\ell_{\rm reg}}\right)
\Bigl(1+\alpha\omega_0+\beta\frac{d_{ij}}{\ell_{\rm reg}}\omega_0+O(\omega_0^2)\Bigr),
\]
where \(\ell_{\rm reg}\propto1/\omega_0\). This formula encodes the hierarchical structure geometrically and supplies the microscopic input for the numerical Yukawa matrices used in the flagship paper.

